A||N||9||Fiero5||Help! 88 headlight problems||||5||
Z||000000||Fiero5||05-09-2001||10:42 PM||||OK, the front parking lights didn't work on the 88. The directionals worked fine only <BR>with the lights off, but not when they were on. We checked the sockets, and the little side metal clip on one was very corroded and almost gone, and on the other it was completely gone. We changed the sockets with one new one and one new about six months ago out of one of our other Fieros. Now the parking lights come on and everything works fine, except the headlights don't have enough power to lift the headlight doors anymore. If<BR>we lift up the hood, the headlights come up all the way. The headlights worked fine and lifted the headlight doors with no problems before we changed the parking/directional sockets in the front nose.<P>Does anyone possibly know what is wrong?<P>Thanks for any help on this.<P>Steve & Russell Kelley||||reg||5
Z||000001||ray b||05-10-2001||12:27 AM||||voltage drop= bad ground clean up connectors<BR>a little lub won't hurt ether but if both it is eltrickal ground||||reg||1
Z||000002||Fiero5||05-10-2001||10:35 AM||||&gt;Bump&lt;<BR><P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/FieroSSsignature1_1.jpg"> ||||reg||5
Z||000003||DRH||05-10-2001||01:29 PM||||I'm with rayb. Check all your grounds in the front end. <P>I believe the 88 motors cut off when the control module senses a certain current draw. Maybe a bad ground could screw up it's calibration???<BR>||||reg||3
Z||000004||ray b||05-10-2001||02:34 PM||||With the parking lites out headlites worked<BR>and now they don't with the parking lites on<BR>so it must be a voltage drop [when volts drop amps go up WATT's LAW]maybe a short but 9 out 10 times its a bad ground somewhere in system do you have a V O M meter to check continuity ? both motor don't go bad a once||||reg||1
Z||000005||sqoach||05-10-2001||02:41 PM||||Sounds like a bad ground to me also.<P>Not related, but when I was putting a cd player in my parents car, the volume could only go so high before it would start flickering and cut off. The factory ground wire was not grounded well, so I just found another place to ground the wire and all is good.<P>------------------<BR>sqoach@yahoo.com<P>            <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/sqoach2.JPG">   <BR>84 SE (project car?)<BR>85 Coupe (parts car)<BR>86 SC (daily driver)||||reg||1
Z||000006||Fiero5||05-10-2001||03:25 PM||||I even took the parking lights back out of the sockets, and the headlights still couldn't push up the doors. So it isn't the bulbs being in the sockets and working now. Like everyone has said so far, it's got to be some kind of bad ground or short in the wiring we just did.<P>Steve<P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/FieroSSsignature1_1.jpg"> ||||reg||4
Z||000007||StuGood||05-10-2001||03:34 PM||||This is mostly just idle curiousity, so ignore me if you wish...  but, try pulling the headlight switch out of the dash, leaving everything still connected.  Put a voltmeter on the white wire at the headlight switch connector.<P>You should get +12v (relative to ground) with the headlight switch off, and 0 volts with HL switch on.  Is that what you get?  ||||reg||5
Z||000008||theogre||05-10-2001||07:41 PM||||The 87+ headlight system is one of the most bullet proof there is.<P>The motors probably need Rodneys rebuild kit. The 87+ motors can work like this when the dowels quit. There's often just enough drag to light them w/o the load of the doors pushing back.<P>One of mine did this when it died. The other one was likely to fail soon. I rebuilt both with Rodneys $10 kit and now they work fine and will last for another 100,000 miles.||||reg||1
Z||000009||Fiero5||05-11-2001||02:28 PM||||OK, my Dad has solved the mystery!  He found that both headlight mech's was just hitting the inside of the door area on the hood. Apparently while working on it the other day, the hood must have slipped down just a bit, and so the headlights weren't hitting the doors cleanly. We re-adjusted the hood and made sure the bolts were good and tight and the headlights work like a charm now.<P>Thanks for all who responded.<P>Steve, Marian & Russell Kelley<P>------------------<BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/FieroSSsignature.jpg"> <BR>http://www.kelleyfamilyfieros.homestead.com/index.html||||reg||10
